 "note": "W2 Stepping-stone falls: a river falls off a rock shelf. An old track crosses it on a footbridge at the top of the falls; below, the road fords it on a zig-zag of stepping stones. A trail climbs each side of the gorge, valley to shelf to top: the dry way round, close to the edge. Bandits hold the left bank: one by the stones, an archer on the shelf over the ford and one by the bridge.",
